From: knoopx <knoopx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] media: gc5035: acquire the INT3472 camera clock as mclk

The probe never obtains a clock for gc5035->mclk, so the field stays NULL:
clk_set_rate() is a no-op and clk_get_rate() reports 0, leaving the sensor
without a master clock ("mclk rate set to 0 instead of requested
192000000" in dmesg on the CHUWI Hi10 Max, 7.2.8 kernel).

The int3472 discrete driver already registers a per-camera clock
("<INT3472:0x>-clk", rate from the sensor SSDB) and publishes it through
clkdev under the sensor's i2c device name. Acquire it as the sensor mclk
and enable it so the clock line is actually driven; the rate is
whatever ACPI SSDB provides (no .set_rate op), which is non-zero on the
CHUWI Hi10 Max.

7.2.8-adapted from the 6.18.54 series: the v7.0 gc5035.c probe context is
byte-identical to the 6.18.54 text, so the hunk body is unchanged; only
the hunk line numbers shift (probe body now starts at line 2081).
gc5035.c already includes <linux/clk.h>.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
---
 gc5035.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gc5035.c b/gc5035.c
--- a/gc5035.c
+++ b/gc5035.c
@@ -2081,6 +2081,11 @@ static int gc5035_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	gc5035->client = client;
 	gc5035_init_power_ctrl(gc5035);
 	gc5035_set_power(gc5035, 1);
+
+	gc5035->mclk = devm_clk_get_enabled(dev, "mclk");
+	if (IS_ERR(gc5035->mclk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(gc5035->mclk),
+				     "Failed to get mclk\n");
 	
 	gc5035->cur_mode = &gc5035_modes[0];
